<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Software on JASMIN on JASMIN Help Site</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/</link><description>Recent content in Software on JASMIN on JASMIN Help Site</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-gb</language><copyright>Copyright © 2025 Science and Technology Facilities Council.</copyright><atom:link href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Additional software</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/additional-software/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/additional-software/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article provides details of additional packages that exist under the&#10;&lt;code&gt;/apps/jasmin/&lt;/code&gt; directory which is available on all scientific analysis&#10;servers and on the LOTUS batch cluster on JASMIN.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Community Software: checksit</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/community-software-checksit/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/community-software-checksit/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview" class="heading "&gt;Overview&lt;a href="#overview" aria-labelledby="overview"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;checksit&lt;/code&gt; is a tool that checks the structure and content of a file against a range of available checks. Checks can be made using either &amp;ldquo;spec&amp;rdquo; files defining rules that objects within a file must meet, or comparison against a template file.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Community Software: ESMValTool</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/community-software-esmvaltool/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/community-software-esmvaltool/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;ESMValTool is installed on JASMIN as a &lt;em&gt;community package&lt;/em&gt;. This article&#10;provides:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;a brief overview of the ESMValTool software&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;a description of the main features of the tool&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;a quick-start for using ESMValTool on JASMIN&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;links to further information&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="overview-of-esmvaltool" class="heading "&gt;Overview of ESMValTool&lt;a href="#overview-of-esmvaltool" aria-labelledby="overview-of-esmvaltool"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Earth System Model Evaluation Tool (ESMValTool) is a community diagnostics&#10;and performance metrics tool for the evaluation of Earth System Models (ESMs)&#10;that allows for routine comparison of single or multiple models, either&#10;against predecessor versions or against observations. The priority of the&#10;effort so far has been to target specific scientific themes focusing on&#10;selected Essential Climate Variables, a range of known systematic biases&#10;common to ESMs, such as coupled tropical climate variability, monsoons,&#10;Southern Ocean processes, continental dry biases and soil hydrology-climate&#10;interactions, as well as atmospheric CO2 budgets, tropospheric and&#10;stratospheric ozone, and tropospheric aerosols.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Compiling and linking</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/compiling-and-linking/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/compiling-and-linking/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction" class="heading "&gt;Introduction&lt;a href="#introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;Jaspy&lt;/a&gt; environment on JASMIN contains the GNU compilers and&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.mpich.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"&gt;MPICH&amp;nbsp;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-up-right-from-square"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, plus a wide range of libraries&#10;from conda-forge that will interoperate with these.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Conda environments and Python virtual environments</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/conda-environments-and-python-virtual-environments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/conda-environments-and-python-virtual-environments/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction" class="heading "&gt;Introduction&lt;a href="#introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This article describes two types of software environments that you can create&#10;in order to install packages for your own use on JASMIN. Typical examples why&#10;you may wish to do this is if you have asked us to add packages to&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;Jaspy&lt;/a&gt; but wish to make use of them before the next release, or&#10;if they are not likely to be relevant to other users.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Conda removal</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/conda-removal/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/conda-removal/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="background" class="heading "&gt;Background&lt;a href="#background" aria-labelledby="background"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Following a change in the licensing conditions by Anaconda, it is now the case&#10;that all users of the Anaconda &lt;code&gt;defaults&lt;/code&gt; Conda package channel (repository)&#10;from organisations of 500 or more employees are potentially liable to pay for&#10;usage, even if it is for the purpose of academic research.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Creating and using miniforge environments</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/creating-and-using-miniforge-environments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/creating-and-using-miniforge-environments/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;On JASMIN, we provide a wide range of packages via the &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;jaspy&lt;/a&gt;&#10;environment (which is itself a Conda environment). This page gives&#10;detail on how to create and use your own personal Conda environments via the&#10;&lt;code&gt;miniforge&lt;/code&gt; installer, as an alternative to the use of Jaspy.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Geocat replaces NCL</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/geocat-replaces-ncl/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/geocat-replaces-ncl/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction" class="heading "&gt;Introduction&lt;a href="#introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This article introduces &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;a href="https://geocat-viz.readthedocs.io/en/latest/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"&gt;geocat&amp;nbsp;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-up-right-from-square"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as a replacement on JASMIN for NCAR Command Language (NCL) which is now deprecated.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>IDL</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/idl/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/idl/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="what-is-idl" class="heading "&gt;What is IDL?&lt;a href="#what-is-idl" aria-labelledby="what-is-idl"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.nv5geospatialsoftware.com/Products/IDL" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"&gt;IDL&amp;nbsp;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-up-right-from-square"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; stands for&#10;Interactive Data Language. It is a licensed data manipulation toolkit made&#10;available on JASMIN.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>JASMIN software FAQs</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jasmin-software-faqs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jasmin-software-faqs/</guid><description>&lt;div id="accordion-default" class="accordion mb-3"&gt;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;div class="accordion-item"&gt;&lt;div id="accordion-default-heading-0" class="accordion-header m-0 fs-2"&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="accordion-button collapsed"&#10; type="button"&#10; data-bs-toggle="collapse"&#10; data-bs-target="#accordion-default-item-0"&#10; aria-expanded="false"&#10; aria-controls="accordion-default-item-0"&#10; &gt;&#10; Why do I have to load/activate a software environment?&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id="accordion-default-item-0" &#10; class="accordion-collapse collapse"&#10; aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-0"&#10; data-bs-parent="#accordion-default"&#10; &gt;&#10; &lt;div class="accordion-body"&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have a range of different users on JASMIN who work on many different&#10;projects. Each project has its own software requirements and timeline. By&#10;providing multiple software environments (such as Python2.7 and Python3.7) we&#10;can support a wider range of users on the same platform. Since we do not&#10;assume a &amp;ldquo;standard&amp;rdquo; environment it is up to the user to &amp;ldquo;load&amp;rdquo; (or &amp;ldquo;activate&amp;rdquo;)&#10;a software environment before usage. This is typically done by using:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Jaspy Software Environments (Python 3, R and other tools)</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/</guid><description>&lt;div class="d-flex alert alert-danger " &#10; role="alert"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pt-1 pe-2"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation fa-2x fa-fw"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-triangle-exclamation fa-2x fa-fw" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-triangle-exclamation"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="flex-grow-1 my-auto"&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Important changes took place in September 2024 affecting what software can be used on JASMIN.&#10;Please read &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.ceda.ac.uk/news/updates/2024/2024-08-29-important-software-changes-autumn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"&gt;this announcement&amp;nbsp;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-up-right-from-square"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; carefully.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Met Office NAME Model</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/name-dispersion-model/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/name-dispersion-model/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article provides links to information about running the Met Office&#10;atmospheric dispersion model, NAME, on JASMIN.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="the-name-atmospheric-dispersion-model" class="heading "&gt;The NAME atmospheric dispersion model&lt;a href="#the-name-atmospheric-dispersion-model" aria-labelledby="the-name-atmospheric-dispersion-model"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Met Office&amp;rsquo;s Numerical Atmospheric-dispersion Modelling Environment (NAME)&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/research/modelling-systems/dispersion-model" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"&gt;https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/research/modelling-systems/dispersion-model&amp;nbsp;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-up-right-from-square fa-2xs" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-up-right-from-square"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; can&#10;be run on JASMIN using the LOTUS cluster. A NAME Group Workspace is&#10;provided to store both the Numerical Weather Prediction (NWP) met data needed&#10;to drive NAME as well as the user outputs derived from NAME itself.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Migration to Rocky Linux 9 2024</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/rocky9-migration-2024/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/rocky9-migration-2024/</guid><description>&lt;div class="d-flex alert alert-success " &#10; role="alert"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pt-1 pe-2"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-circle-exclamation fa-2x fa-fw"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-circle-exclamation fa-2x fa-fw" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 512 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-circle-exclamation"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="flex-grow-1 my-auto"&gt;&#10; Lots of updated information below about the new Rocky Linux 9 environment on JASMIN: please read, and keep checking back here regularly for now.&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="introduction" class="heading "&gt;Introduction&lt;a href="#introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;As with a previous migration completed in 2020, the change of operating system version is needed to make sure that the version in use is current and fully supported, i.e. that package updates are available and important security updates can be obtained and applied to keep the platform secure.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Postgres databases on request</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/postgres-databases-on-request/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/postgres-databases-on-request/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction" class="heading "&gt;Introduction&lt;a href="#introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This article explains that users may request access to a PostgreSQL (known as&#10;Postgres) database on JASMIN for use with scientific workflows.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Python Virtual Environments</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/python-virtual-environments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/python-virtual-environments/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article describes how to create Python virtual environments on JASMIN to install&#10;custom packages not provided in the&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/software-overview/"&gt;common software environments&lt;/a&gt;. Virtual environments allow you to&#10;use different packages/versions from those installed system-wide.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Quickstart for activating/deactivating software environments</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/quickstart-software-envs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/quickstart-software-envs/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article provides a minimum quick-start guide for working with software environments on JASMIN.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="d-flex alert alert-info " &#10; role="alert"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pt-1 pe-2"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fa fa-lightbulb fa-2x fa-fw"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fa fa-lightbulb fa-2x fa-fw" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 384 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fa-lightbulb"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="flex-grow-1 my-auto"&gt;&#10; &lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; The &lt;code&gt;module&lt;/code&gt; commands described here are for use on scientific analysis servers&#10;and LOTUS. They do not work in the &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/interactive-computing/jasmin-notebooks-service/"&gt;JASMIN Notebook Service&lt;/a&gt;,&#10;where Jaspy and JasR are available by default. In notebooks, use &lt;code&gt;conda activate&lt;/code&gt; to&#10;access different versions.&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="activate-load-an-environment" class="heading "&gt;Activate (load) an environment&lt;a href="#activate-load-an-environment" aria-labelledby="activate-load-an-environment"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To activate an environment containing the &amp;ldquo;current&amp;rdquo; common software packages&#10;(including a modern Python):&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Running python on JASMIN</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/running-python-on-jasmin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/running-python-on-jasmin/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;On the JASMIN &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/interactive-computing/sci-servers/"&gt;scientific analysis servers&lt;/a&gt; and on the Lotus batch cluster, we currently support Python version 3.11 with &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;Jaspy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When you first log in, the default version of Python is that provided by the&#10;operating system. This is different to the one you shoud use for your work,&#10;and we recommend using the &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;Jaspy environments&lt;/a&gt;. In this example, we&#10;activate the current Jaspy environment before running Python.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Running R on JASMIN</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/running-r-on-jasmin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/running-r-on-jasmin/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;On the JASMIN &lt;code&gt;sci&lt;/code&gt; servers and LOTUS, we support the use of &lt;strong&gt;R&lt;/strong&gt; through the&#10;&amp;ldquo;jasr&amp;rdquo; environment(s), as listed on the &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;Jaspy page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sharing software environments</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/share-software-envs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/share-software-envs/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article explains how you can share software environments with other users&#10;on JASMIN.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="what-is-a-software-environment" class="heading "&gt;What is a software environment?&lt;a href="#what-is-a-software-environment" aria-labelledby="what-is-a-software-environment"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A software environment is typically a collection of files and directories&#10;associated with a set of environment variables that allows a given session to&#10;access them. In the context of JASMIN, there are a number of Python/other&#10;environments already available on the system. See the&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jaspy-envs/"&gt;Jaspy page&lt;/a&gt; for examples of these.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Software Overview</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/software-overview/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/software-overview/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;JASMIN is a large platform where a range of software tools, packages and&#10;environments are available. Many users employ software already installed on&#10;JASMIN whilst some need to install their own tools for a particular purpose.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The "jasmin-sci" software environment</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jasmin-sci-software-environment/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/jasmin-sci-software-environment/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction" class="heading "&gt;Introduction&lt;a href="#introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;!-- &lt;i class="fas fa-link anchor"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; --&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="svg-inline--fa fas fa-link anchor" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" role="img" viewBox="0 0 576 512"&gt;&lt;use href="#fas-link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&amp;nbsp;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This article describes the &lt;code&gt;jasmin-sci&lt;/code&gt; software environment on JASMIN. It&#10;covers the following topics:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Using Matplotlib for visualisation on JASMIN</title><link>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/matplotlib/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://help.jasmin.ac.uk/docs/software-on-jasmin/matplotlib/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This article provides a basic example of using Matplotlib on JASMIN to&#10;generate a plot. It also gives an important tip that may stop your code&#10;failing when run on the LOTUS cluster.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>